  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_CHAPTER5_DIAGRAM_Q01 - Punnett square interpretation of test cross</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>Based on the Punnett square shown below for a test cross in pea plants (where violet flower colour \(W\) is dominant over white flower colour \(w\)), what is the genotype of the unknown parent with the dominant phenotype?</p>
      <p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 460 280" width="460" height="280" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #ffffff;">
          <rect x="10" y="10" width="440" height="260" rx="8" fill="#fafafa" stroke="#cccccc" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="230" y="36" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#222222">Test Cross: Unknown Violet (?) × Homozygous Recessive White (ww)</text>
          
          <!-- Gamete headers top (ww parent) -->
          <text x="245" y="65" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#444444">Gametes from ww parent</text>
          <circle cx="205" cy="90" r="16" fill="#f0f0f0" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="205" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222222">w</text>
          <circle cx="285" cy="90" r="16" fill="#f0f0f0" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="285" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222222">w</text>

          <!-- Gamete headers left (unknown parent) -->
          <text x="72" y="150" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#444444">Unknown</text>
          <text x="72" y="166" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#444444">gametes</text>
          <circle cx="135" cy="145" r="16" fill="#e8d8f0" stroke="#6a1b9a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="135" y="150" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#4a148c">?</text>
          <circle cx="135" cy="215" r="16" fill="#e8d8f0" stroke="#6a1b9a" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="135" y="220" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#4a148c">?</text>

          <!-- 2x2 Punnett Grid -->
          <rect x="165" y="115" width="80" height="65" fill="#d1b3e0" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="205" y="145" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#2c003e">Ww</text>
          <text x="205" y="165" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#2c003e">(Violet)</text>

          <rect x="245" y="115" width="80" height="65" fill="#d1b3e0" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="285" y="145" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#2c003e">Ww</text>
          <text x="285" y="165" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#2c003e">(Violet)</text>

          <rect x="165" y="180" width="80" height="65" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="205" y="210" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#333333">ww</text>
          <text x="205" y="230" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#333333">(White)</text>

          <rect x="245" y="180" width="80" height="65" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="285" y="210" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#333333">ww</text>
          <text x="285" y="230" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#333333">(White)</text>

          <!-- Summary -->
          <text x="385" y="165" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#333333">Progeny Ratio:</text>
          <text x="385" y="185" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#4a148c">50% Violet</text>
          <text x="385" y="203" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#333333">50% White</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>In the given Punnett square, a pea plant with a dominant violet flower phenotype (unknown genotype) is crossed with a homozygous recessive white-flowered plant of genotype \(ww\). The resulting offspring show \(50\%\) violet flowers (\(Ww\)) and \(50\%\) white flowers (\(ww\)).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Diagram Interpretation</strong><br/>According to the Mendelian convention stated, \(W\) is the dominant allele for violet colour and \(w\) is the recessive allele for white colour. Each box in the \(2 \times 2\) Punnett square represents a fertilisation event combining one gamete from the top row (\(ww\) parent) and one gamete from the left column (unknown parent).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/>By Mendel's Law of Segregation, a diploid parent separates its two alleles into gametes in equal proportions during meiosis. A homozygous recessive parent (\(ww\)) produces only \(w\) gametes.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>Since the top row gametes are both \(w\), the first row of offspring has genotype \(Ww\), which means the first unknown gamete must carry the allele \(W\). The second row of offspring has genotype \(ww\), which means the second unknown gamete must carry the allele \(w\). Therefore, the unknown parent produces two types of gametes, \(W\) and \(w\), in equal proportion (\(1:1\)), which is only possible if its genotype is heterozygous \(Ww\).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>Had the unknown parent been homozygous dominant (\(WW\)), all gametes would be \(W\) and \(100\%\) of the progeny would be \(Ww\) (violet). Since half the progeny are white (\(ww\)), the unknown parent must be heterozygous. The final answer is \(Ww\).</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
