  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_CHAPTER5_DIAGRAM_Q03 - Haplodiploid sex determination in honey bee</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>In the schematic diagram representing sex determination in honey bees below, identify Process <strong>X</strong> (gamete formation in males) and Process <strong>Y</strong> (development of an unfertilised egg into a male).</p>
      <p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 460 270" width="460" height="270" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background: #ffffff;">
          <rect x="10" y="10" width="440" height="250" rx="8" fill="#fafafa" stroke="#cccccc" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <defs>
            <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path d="M 0 1 L 10 5 L 0 9 z" fill="#333333"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <!-- Parents -->
          <text x="55" y="48" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#333333">Parents:</text>
          <text x="175" y="42" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222222">Female</text>
          <text x="175" y="58" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#444444">(32 chromosomes)</text>

          <text x="365" y="42" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222222">Male</text>
          <text x="365" y="58" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#444444">(16 chromosomes)</text>

          <!-- Arrows to Gametes -->
          <line x1="175" y1="65" x2="175" y2="95" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
          <text x="168" y="84" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#1565c0" font-weight="bold">Meiosis</text>

          <line x1="365" y1="65" x2="365" y2="95" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
          <text x="373" y="84" text-anchor="start" font-size="12" fill="#c62828" font-weight="bold">Process X</text>

          <!-- Gametes -->
          <text x="55" y="128" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#333333">Gametes:</text>
          <circle cx="145" cy="124" r="18" fill="#e3f2fd" stroke="#1565c0" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="145" y="129" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#0d47a1">16</text>

          <circle cx="205" cy="124" r="18" fill="#e3f2fd" stroke="#1565c0" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="205" y="129" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#0d47a1">16</text>

          <circle cx="365" cy="124" r="18" fill="#ffebee" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="365" y="129" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#b71c1c">16</text>

          <!-- Arrows to F1 -->
          <!-- Unfertilised egg to Male -->
          <line x1="145" y1="145" x2="145" y2="195" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
          <text x="138" y="175" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" fill="#c62828" font-weight="bold">Process Y</text>

          <!-- Fertilisation to Female -->
          <line x1="205" y1="145" x2="275" y2="195" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
          <line x1="365" y1="145" x2="295" y2="195" stroke="#333333" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>
          <text x="285" y="168" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#2e7d32" font-weight="bold">Fertilisation</text>

          <!-- F1 -->
          <text x="55" y="220" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#333333">F₁:</text>
          <text x="145" y="218" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222222">Male</text>
          <text x="145" y="235" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#444444">(16 chromosomes)</text>

          <text x="285" y="218" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222222">Female</text>
          <text x="285" y="235" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#444444">(32 chromosomes)</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The diagram shows the haplodiploid sex-determination system in honey bees. Female parents are diploid with \(32\) chromosomes and produce haploid eggs with \(16\) chromosomes by meiosis. Male parents are haploid with \(16\) chromosomes and produce sperm with \(16\) chromosomes via Process \(X\). An unfertilised egg (\(16\)) develops into a male (\(16\)) via Process \(Y\), while fertilisation of an egg (\(16\)) by a sperm (\(16\)) produces a diploid female (\(32\)).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Diagram Interpretation</strong><br/>Arrows indicate the transition from parental cells to gametes and from gametes to \(F_1\) offspring, with chromosome numbers maintained or halved according to the type of cell division or development.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/>In a haploid organism (\(n = 16\)), chromosome number cannot be halved further by meiosis; therefore, gametes must be produced by equational division (mitosis). Development of a new individual from an unfertilised egg without fusion with a male gamete is known as parthenogenesis.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>For Process \(X\), a haploid male (\(16\) chromosomes) produces haploid sperm (\(16\) chromosomes), so the chromosome number remains unchanged; hence Process \(X\) is mitosis. For Process \(Y\), a single unfertilised egg (\(16\) chromosomes) develops directly into a haploid male (\(16\) chromosomes) without fertilisation; hence Process \(Y\) is parthenogenesis.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>Both processes preserve the haploid chromosome count of \(16\) in the male line. Thus, Process \(X\) is mitosis and Process \(Y\) is parthenogenesis.</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
